  "description": "meme-id: say_allahu_akbar_again; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a soldier in combat gear holding a rifle with a scope, set against a plain white background. The text overlay reads \"say allahu akbar again...\" at the top and \"...go ahead...say it!\" at the bottom. The overall intent is to provoke or mock the phrase \"Allahu Akbar\" by juxtaposing it with a militarized, aggressive visual of a soldier. This creates an analogical mapping that equates the religious phrase with violence or terrorism, which is a form of hateful content targeting Muslims. The meme is designed to incite hostility or fear toward Muslims by associating the phrase with military aggression, thereby promoting Islamophobia. The intent is not to inform or educate, but to spread prejudice and negative stereotypes about Muslims by linking their religious expression to violence.",
